   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 486 of the laws of 1964, establishing and constituting as a separate union free school district certain territory in the town of Canaan in the county of Columbia, and providing for its government, in relation to making technical amendments thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S5334",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5334-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2-a, Chap 486 of 1964",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5334                REVISED 6/4/15\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 486 of the laws of 1964,\nestablishing and constituting as a separate union free school district\ncertain territory in the town of Canaan in the county of Columbia, and\nproviding for its government, in relation to making technical\namendments thereto\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL: To establish and allow the Berkshire\nUnion Free School District, located in the town of Canaan, to operate\neducational programs at the Berkshire Union Free School District's\nleased facility located at 11 Warren Street, Hudson, New York 12534.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS: Amends chapter 486 of the laws of\n1964, as amended by chapter 337 of the Laws of 2013, to authorize such\nschool district to provide educational programs at 11 Warren Street,\nHudson, New York 12534.\n\nJUSTIFICATION: In 1964, by Special Act of the New York State\nLegislature, Berkshire Union Free School District was organized to\nprovide public education services to the youth in residence at\nBerkshire Farm Center in the town of Canaan, county of Columbia In\n2013, the District was authorized to provide educational services at a\nleased facility located at 364 Warren Street in Hudson, New York.  The\nDistrict now has the need and opportunity to move the program to a\nlarger leased facility on the same street This bill amends the\nprovision of the 2013 amendment solely in regard to the street address\n- to replace 364 Warren Street with 11 Warren Street. This change will\nallow the District to continue and grow its very successful Bridge\nprogram for at-risk students.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY: This is a new bill to update the address of\nthe school to the new location, 11 Warren Street in Hudson NY.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None to the state.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
