    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 297\n\nTO THE SENATE:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nSenate Bill Number 5334, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  to amend chapter 486 of the laws of 1964, establishing and\n      constituting as a separate  union  free  school  district  certain\n      territory  in  the  town  of Canaan in the county of Columbia, and\n      providing for its government,  in  relation  to  making  technical\n      amendments thereto\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  Berkshire Union Free School District (Berkshire UFSD) is a Special Act\nschool district offering educational services to youth in Columbia Coun-\nty. The legislation creating Berkshire UFSD (L. 1964, c. 486) delineates\nthe district's territorial limits and does not authorize the district to\nutilize property outside of those boundaries.\n\n  In 2013, the State enacted legislation at the request of the Berkshire\nUFSD  authorizing  the  district  to  provide  educational services at a\nfacility located at 364 Warren Street  in  Hudson  (L.  2013,  c.  337).\nSubsequent  to  this  authority,  the district has offered a program for\nat-risk youth at the 364 Warren Street address. According to the  school\ndistrict, the program has been growing and needs to be moved to a larger\nspace. This legislation would amend the 2013 law to allow Berkshire UFSD\nto  offer  educational services at 11 Warren Street instead. The move is\nanticipated to happen no earlier than Spring 2016.\n\n  However, this bill has a fatal drafting error in its  effective  date.\nEffective  immediately,  the bill would revoke Berkshire UFSD's authori-\nzation to operate a program at 364 Warren Street and only  authorize  it\nto  operate at 11 Warren Street. However, the school will still be oper-\nating a program at 364 Warren Street for at least  several  months  into\n2016, and thus signing this bill would prohibit the school from continu-\ning to operate at its current site. The Legislature agrees that an unan-\nticipated  closure  of  this  program would be an untenable result. Thus\nwhile I am constrained to veto this bill, I will direct my staff to work\nwith the sponsors on this issue during the upcoming legislative session.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                               __________\n",
